# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
bin/

# Helm chart build artefacts — canonical source lives elsewhere:
# - deploy/helm/olaitan/files/olaitan.yaml is a copy of config/olaitan.yaml,
#   produced by `make helm-prepare` (see deploy/helm/README.md).
# - deploy/helm/olaitan/charts/ holds subchart tarballs fetched by
#   `helm dependency update`; regenerated on every chart build.
#
# Chart.lock IS committed (NOT gitignored) — Chart.yaml pins the SemVer
# of each subchart but Chart.lock pins the digest. Without the lockfile
# under version control, a re-tagged subchart at the same version (e.g.
# Bitnami's mid-2025 retag) silently changes the rendered manifest stream
# on the next CI run, defeating NFR13 reproducibility.
deploy/helm/olaitan/files/
deploy/helm/olaitan/charts/

# Spike binaries — `go run` and `go build` may drop a binary named after
# the directory (e.g. `spikes/sigma-parser/wrap/wrap`). The source lives
# under spikes/<name>/{wrap,custom}/main.go; the binary should not.
spikes/sigma-parser/wrap/wrap
spikes/sigma-parser/custom/custom

# Root build binary — `go build ./cmd/olaitan` from the repo root drops an
# `olaitan` ELF here. The binary is never committed; the source is cmd/olaitan/.
/olaitan

# Claude Code transient agent worktrees
.claude/worktrees/
